# Push to main

After completing code changes the user requested (or clearly implied), commit and push to **`main`** on `origin` unless they say otherwise.

- Use `git push origin master:main` (local branch may be `master`) or push `main` directly if checked out.
- Do not push secrets (`.env`, real keys in `config.js`).
- Only skip pushing when the user explicitly says not to commit/push, or when there are no changes to push.

Briefly confirm the commit message and that the push succeeded.
